Package: panelaR
Title: Diagnose Panel Structure in Latin American Labor Force Surveys
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Carlos", "Toruño", , "carlostor@iadb.org", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Links respondents across waves of rotating-panel household
    surveys in Latin America and measures how well that linkage holds. Many
    national labor force surveys re-interview the same dwellings over several
    waves, but the resulting panel is rarely documented or validated:
    identifiers get reused, households get renumbered, and roster lines get
    reshuffled. Cross-wave links are built in two tiers, first trusting the
    survey's own person identifier where sex and age gaps corroborate it, then
    fuzzy-matching the residual within each dwelling. Diagnostics are reported
    at the wave level so users can judge whether a survey's panel matches its
    own design. Currently supports 'ENEMDU' (Ecuador), 'ENE' (Chile) and 'ENOE'
    (Mexico), including helpers to download the microdata from the national
    statistical offices.
